{
  "_about": "Starting palettes by mood. Roles: page = bare paper stock (paths, light patches); ground = the printed ground [light, dark], authored paler and greyer than the cards (in the frame ~0.16-0.22 brighter and ~0.16-0.25 less saturated) so the pieces carry the colour; subject = the lead family of the main pieces (warm by default); accent = one small note of life or light (warm by default); water = [light, deep]; ink = linework (never black); leak = what shadows let through (warm amber by day on warm ground); haze = distance colour (display space, subtle, far only); key / fill = light colours (the fill comes from the camera side). dusk-violet and lantern-night are storybook-autumn re-lit with the 3D template's dusk and night sets: re-light any palette the same way (swap key, fill, leak and haze, keep the rest). The cut edge is not a palette colour: P.rim() derives it from each print. Every piece also gets 1-2 contrasting accents of its own (accentsFor is only a fallback). Restyle freely: derive your own with references/palettes.md.",
